    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8778" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏartātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏarct-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		coarto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a drawing</i> or <i>crowding together</i>
			(rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laxatio aut coartatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 9,
					9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plurium in angusto tendentium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					27, 46, 2</span></i>
			; so, militum eo loco, Auct. B. Alex. 74 <i>fin.</i></div>
